1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,023
A lower posture command does not instantly lower the robot.

2
00:00:05,573 --> 00:00:10,330
Queued commands and finite response determine when the body changes.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:16,725
We predict an enclosing cylinder whose
height and radius follow that execution.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,831
Checking predicted poses alone can miss contact between them.

5
00:00:23,381 --> 00:00:29,141
We enlarge endpoint envelopes using bounded motion and shape-change rates.

6
00:00:29,691 --> 00:00:36,219
Their union covers the intervening body sweep,
so clearance is checked over the entire interval.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,385
The filter coordinates motion and posture, then verifies dispatch.

8
00:00:42,856 --> 00:00:50,600
The clearance guarantee requires valid coverage,
support, map, and timing bounds, with static obstacles.

